          "answer_sanskrit": "विष्णुपुराणात् भक्तध्रुवस्य कथा:\nउत्तानपादस्य राजा आसीत्। तस्य सुनीतिः सुरुचिः इति द्वे भार्ये आस्ताम्। सुरुच्याः वचनेन सुनीतेः पुत्रः ध्रुवः पितुः अङ्के उपवेष्टुं न प्राप्नोत्। पञ्चवर्षीयः ध्रुवः वनं गत्वा भगवन्तं विष्णुं ध्यायन् कठोरं तपः अकरोत्। तस्य अनन्यभक्त्या प्रसन्नः श्रीहरिः प्रादुर्भूय तस्मै 'ध्रुवतारा' इति अचलपदं प्रादात्। अद्यापि सः आकाशे उत्तरे दिशि प्रकाशते।",
          "meaning": "Question 2: Collect any one story from the Puranas, write it down, and narrate it to the class.\nAnswer: Story of Devotee Dhruva (from Vishnu Purana):\nKing Uttanapada had two queens, Suniti and Suruchi. Due to Suruchi's harsh words, Suniti's 5-year-old son Dhruva was forbidden to sit in his father's lap. The young boy went into the forest and undertook rigorous penance meditating on Lord Vishnu. Pleased by his unswerving devotion, Lord Vishnu appeared and blessed him with an eternal station as the Pole Star (Dhruva Tara), which shines unmoving in the northern sky.",
